in the early hours of this morning  following a call from neighbours  officers forced entry into a house here  in delaford road  inside the house they made a dreadful  discovery  of four people  who had been stabbed  despite the best efforts of officers and  paramedics  all four people were sadly pronounced  dead at the scene  i can confirm that the deceased were  three women  believed to be aged in their mid-60s 40s  and 30s  and one man believed to be aged in their  mid-60s  i want to offer my heartfelt condolences  to the family and friends of all those  concerned  this is a deeply shocking incident  and we will do everything we can to  provide support to everyone affected  at this difficult time  a man in his late 20s was arrested at  the address on suspicion of murder  and he is currently in custody  and at this early stage we're not  looking for any other person  we believe that all those involved may  have been known to each other  this is a terrible incident and i fully  understand the concern  communities will have  we are working closely with our partners  and local community groups to keep  everyone informed  your local officers will be in the area  to offer reassurance  so please speak to them they're there  for you to listen  and to act on your concerns  homicide detectives have launched an  investigation into these terrible events  so please assist them by avoiding  unhelpful speculation and allow them  time to uncover the evidence  such terrible events are rare  but this will not diminish the shock  that we felt across london and beyond  and i can assure you this investigation  will be thorough to ensure justice for  the victims and their families and the  community  anyone who has information in relation  to this should contact the police
 

